BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Perils and Promises of Artificial Intelligence
DTSTART:20260819T183000
DTEND:20260819T200000
DTSTAMP:20260819T114537Z
UID:bf1a66ac5daa1f4ab4caa4673ae33c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Whether you are a regular user of AI or a concerned skeptic or
  both\, you will learn something from this informative and provocative dis
 cussion about the emerging role of AI in our lives. The panel members incl
 ude diverse voices: Marc Natanagara\, aiVermont Theresa White\, educator T
 ayo Kirchhoff\, Gifford Medical Center Dan O'Brien\, a mindful user of AI 
 Chris Soares\, a well informed thinker on the topic The panel will cover m
 any issues including: What is AI? How can it serve us well? What are the r
 isks of AI? Are there dangers lurking in a future with AI? Plus\, attendee
 s' questions and thoughts.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Brookfield Old Town Hall\, 93 Stone Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/the-perils
 -and-promises-of-artificial-intelligence-09-08-2026-10-20-38
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wagner in Vermont 2026: Tristan\, Dutchman\, Parsifal
DTSTART:20260819T160000
DTEND:20260819T200000
DTSTAMP:20260819T114537Z
UID:8c4d82385dcf1e882da95f0dc3950c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Wagner in Vermont returns for 2026\, bringing a brand new prod
 uction of Tristan und Isolde to the Latchis Theatre\, as well as taking on
  Der fliegende Holländer (The Flying Dutchman) and Parsifal Act II for th
 e first time. The festival week 14-19 August is filled with events for mus
 ic and theatre lovers\, including talks and lectures on Wagner's music and
  other related topics\, other staged adaptations of Wagner's works\, as we
 ll as concerts and recitals. Come to Brattleboro VT\, and immerse yourself
  in an epic week of Wagnerian drama like none other in the world! Event Sc
 hedule: 14th August - Festival Opens - Tristan und Isolde 4pm 15th August 
 - Lecture 1pm - Unshielded: Adapted from Der Ring des Nibelungen 3pm 16th 
 August - Lecture 1pm - Der fliegende Holländer 3pm 17th August - Lecture 
 1pm - Not all who wander are lost: Scenes Showcase 3pm - Parsifal Act II 7
 pm 18th August - Qs with Hugh 1pm - I've crossed oceans of time to find yo
 u: Scenes Showcase 3pm - Liederabend 7pm 19th August - Tristan und Isolde 
 1pm\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Latchis Theater\, 50 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/wagner-in-
 vermont-2026-tristan-dutchman-parsifal-11-06-2026-16-43-01
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bamboozled
DTSTART:20260820T190000
DTEND:20260820T211500
DTSTAMP:20260819T114537Z
UID:587e768cb7c99b5892eef053f61d28@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:With this blisteringly funny\, unapologetically confrontationa
 l satire\, writer-director Spike Lee examined the past\, present\, and fut
 ure of racism in American popular culture\, issuing a daring provocation t
 o creators and consumers alike—so on-point that it’s sometimes hard to
  watch. Bamboozled might be a bit hit-and-miss\, but the hits are devastat
 ing. Using its Producers-ish premise to horrifying effect\, Bamboozled tel
 ls the story of academic television writer Pierre Delacroix (Damon Wayans)
 \, who’s been assigned with rescuing his network’s flagging ratings. H
 is explosively offensive solution? Bring back blackface. To his horror\, t
 he white network executives love it\, and so do audiences: The New Millenn
 ium Minstrel Show is a hit\, forcing Pierre and his collaborators to confr
 ont their public’s insatiable appetite for dehumanizing stereotypes. Fea
 turing Savion Glover\, Jada Pinkett Smith\, Tommy Davidson\, Mos Def\, and
  Paul Mooney\, Bamboozled is a stinging indictment of mass entertainment a
 t the turn of the 21st century that looks more damning with each passing y
 ear.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Main Street Landing Film House\, 60 Lake St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/bamboozled
 -11-08-2026-15-30-28
END:VEVENT
